# Cloudflare Pages header rules.
#
# The bug this fixes: HTML documents had no explicit Cache-Control, so
# browsers cached them heuristically. After a deploy the browser would
# replay the OLD html, which references the old build's hashed chunks —
# and those no longer exist on the production alias, so every asset came
# back 404 and the app rendered unstyled or threw a hydration error.
#
# Rule: the document must always be revalidated, the hashed assets can be
# cached forever (their names change when their contents change).

/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin

/_next/static/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
